For an international organization in New York, we are urgently looking for a Full Remote Senior API Developer - Azure. As Full Remote Senior API Developer, you are responsible for the design, creation, and delivery of a range of supporting APIs and Azure platform elements to support the implementation of a central API system for data synchronization/exchange between data platforms in a hub and spoke architecture model.

Candidates need to be able to work 4/5 hours per day in the normal office hours of New York, US. Example 9AM NY time equals 7:30PM. This role is open for employees and contractors

Tasks and responsibilities:

• Analyze, design, develop, as well as implement RESTful services and APIs;

• Be involved in the development life cycle and perform definition and feasibility analysis;

• Implement, integrate, and document a variety of software platforms through the REST API framework;

• Apply the latest software design techniques and contribute to the technical design of new solutions;

• Modify existing programs, prepare test data and functional specifications;

• Troubleshoot issues and solve problems, identify potential process improvement areas;

• Implement common APIs based on architecture guidelines and frameworks;

• Write object-oriented, clean, and maintainable code;

• Deliver quality results on time with minimal supervision;

Profile:

​

• Bachelor or Master degree;

• +2 years of experience in a computing environment with multiple programming languages (Python, Java, JavaScript, Node.js etc.);

• +1 year of experience with Azure Cloud portal;

• Proficiency in working with Azure Data Factory, Azure Data Lake is required;

• Familiarity with code versioning tools, like Git, SVN, and Mercurial is required;

• Experience in creating REST API documentation using Swagger and YAML or similar tools is desirable;

• Experience with Azure DevOps and Azure Purview is a plus;

• Any professional certifications encouraged;

• Fluent in English;

